ee9cb8fcc220"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Tip:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \nTo get the Greek letter mu above we have several options\n1) use the \
syntax :\n\t\\[x] \nand replace \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]x\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] with the name of the Greek letter in capital \
letters, e.g. replace \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]x\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] with \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Mu\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] gives a lowercase mu, \
\[Mu].\n2) use keyboard shortcuts:\n\tesc m esc\ngives \[Mu].\nFor \[Psi] \
type:\n\tesc psi esc\n3) Using palettes. Select Insert from the Default \
toolbar at the top of the page. (Make sure the Default toolbar appears at the \
top with \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Evaluation\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] at the top \
left, and Insert at the top right. If not, from the main menu, Window, \
Toolbar, select Default.)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.963194968498844*^9, 3.9631951170094557`*^9}, {
   3.963195151363327*^9, 3.963195153501737*^9}, 3.963195193447967*^9, {
